% Plastics rulings of U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CROSS, rulings.cbp.gov)
% run through the plastics model (plastics.le, which includes gri.le).
%
% One scenario per ruling; each article is described by the facts the ruling
% states, citing it; the office's judgments — the principal use, the essential
% character of a composite good or set, the answer to a claim that the article
% belongs to a heading outside the model — carry who made them and why. The
% ruling's code is NOT a fact: the expectation is the six-digit subheading the
% model derives from them.
% Selection: the most recent rulings returned by CROSS for 3923.21-90,
% 3924.10-90 and 3926.20-90 (September 2026). Rulings N360188-N360191 are one
% bag imported from four countries. See README.md for the method and results.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base plastics cbp includes these resources:
    plastics.

the knowledge base plastics cbp includes:

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% The bowl clamp turns on CBP's judgment of its principal use: which judgment
% would have put it in heading 3924, as the importer asked?
query household is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        the heading of the self-feeding bowl clamp is 3924.

% NY N363384 (July 2026): a men's faux leather jacket from China.
scenario ny_n363384 is:
    style CB81426 is a manufactured article, as stated in ruling NY N363384.
    style CB81426 is of cellular plastics reinforced by a textile fabric,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363384,
        because "the outer shell is cellular polyurethane with a polyester woven backing present merely for reinforcement purposes".
    the principal use of style CB81426 is apparel,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363384,
        because "a men's jacket".
    style CB81426 is claimed to belong to garments of heading 6210, as stated in ruling NY N363384.
    the claim that style CB81426 belongs to garments of heading 6210 is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363384,
        because "the textile fabric backing is present merely for reinforcing the cellular plastic (Chapter 59 note 2(a)(5)): the jacket is apparel of plastic material of Chapter 39".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style CB81426 is 3926.20"].

% NY N363522 (July 2026): four cellphone cases from Canada.
scenario ny_n363522 is:
    the G10 bezel case is a manufactured article, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 bezel case is a composite good, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the G10 bezel case is a component of the G10 bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 bezel of the G10 bezel case is a component of the G10 bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the G10 bezel case is made of plastics, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the essential character of the G10 bezel case is given by the G10 rear housing of the G10 bezel case,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "the plastic provides the impact protection and predominates over the bezel materials (GRI 3(b))".
    the principal use of the G10 bezel case is protecting a mobile phone,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "a fitted protective case for a mobile phone".
    the G10 bezel case is claimed to belong to cases of heading 4202, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the claim that the G10 bezel case belongs to cases of heading 4202 is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "per HQ H297451 such cellphone cases are not classified under heading 4202 but by their constituent materials".
    the aluminium bezel case is a manufactured article, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the aluminium bezel case is a composite good, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the aluminium bezel case is a component of the aluminium bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the aluminium bezel of the aluminium bezel case is a component of the aluminium bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the aluminium bezel case is made of plastics, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the essential character of the aluminium bezel case is given by the G10 rear housing of the aluminium bezel case,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "the plastic provides the impact protection and predominates over the bezel materials (GRI 3(b))".
    the principal use of the aluminium bezel case is protecting a mobile phone,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "a fitted protective case for a mobile phone".
    the aluminium bezel case is claimed to belong to cases of heading 4202, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the claim that the aluminium bezel case belongs to cases of heading 4202 is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "per HQ H297451 such cellphone cases are not classified under heading 4202 but by their constituent materials".
    the stainless steel bezel case is a manufactured article, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the stainless steel bezel case is a composite good, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the stainless steel bezel case is a component of the stainless steel bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the stainless steel bezel of the stainless steel bezel case is a component of the stainless steel bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the stainless steel bezel case is made of plastics, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the essential character of the stainless steel bezel case is given by the G10 rear housing of the stainless steel bezel case,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "the plastic provides the impact protection and predominates over the bezel materials (GRI 3(b))".
    the principal use of the stainless steel bezel case is protecting a mobile phone,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "a fitted protective case for a mobile phone".
    the stainless steel bezel case is claimed to belong to cases of heading 4202, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the claim that the stainless steel bezel case belongs to cases of heading 4202 is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "per HQ H297451 such cellphone cases are not classified under heading 4202 but by their constituent materials".
    the titanium bezel case is a manufactured article, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the titanium bezel case is a composite good, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the titanium bezel case is a component of the titanium bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the titanium bezel of the titanium bezel case is a component of the titanium bezel case, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the G10 rear housing of the titanium bezel case is made of plastics, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the essential character of the titanium bezel case is given by the G10 rear housing of the titanium bezel case,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "the plastic provides the impact protection and predominates over the bezel materials (GRI 3(b))".
    the principal use of the titanium bezel case is protecting a mobile phone,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "a fitted protective case for a mobile phone".
    the titanium bezel case is claimed to belong to cases of heading 4202, as stated in ruling NY N363522.
    the claim that the titanium bezel case belongs to cases of heading 4202 is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363522,
        because "per HQ H297451 such cellphone cases are not classified under heading 4202 but by their constituent materials".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the G10 bezel case is 3926.90",
        "the subheading of the aluminium bezel case is 3926.90",
        "the subheading of the stainless steel bezel case is 3926.90",
        "the subheading of the titanium bezel case is 3926.90"].

